<title>INDIA: List of Indian states raising loan on January 20.</title>
<headline>List of Indian states raising loan on January 20.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twenty-five Indian states are raising loans worth 16.09 billion rupees on January 20, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The loans will bear interest at 13.75 percent per annum for a 10 year maturity, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The state-wise allocation is as under:</p>
<p>State		     Amount</p>
<p>			   (Rs. Mln)</p>
<p>------------------------------</p>
<p>Andhra Pradesh	   481.50</p>
<p>Arunachal Pradesh	 04.70</p>
<p>Assam			162.60</p>
<p>Bihar		     2490.10</p>
<p>Goa			   17.50</p>
<p>Gujarat		   1566.00</p>
<p>Haryana		    133.90</p>
<p>Himachal Pradesh	  40.00</p>
<p>Jammu &amp; Kashmir	   72.40</p>
<p>Karnataka		  211.80</p>
<p>Kerala		     345.60</p>
<p>Madhya Pradesh	   815.60</p>
<p>Maharashtra		425.80</p>
<p>Manipur		     16.00</p>
<p>Meghalaya		   25.00</p>
<p>Mizoram		     15.00</p>
<p>Nagaland		    39.70</p>
<p>Orissa		     734.80</p>
<p>Punjab		     221.20</p>
<p>Rajasthan		  394.30</p>
<p>Sikkim			15.60</p>
<p>Tamil Nadu		2337.60</p>
<p>Tripura		     17.90</p>
<p>Uttar Pradesh	   5061.60</p>
<p>West Bengal		447.40</p>
<p>			-----------</p>
<p>Total   .....	 16,093.60</p>
<p>			-----------</p>
<p>Interest will be paid half-yearly on July 20th and January 20th each year. The loans will be redeemable at par on January 20, 2007, the statement said.</p>
